From 933fc0546e7771ff7f94e2de7cbdd64d081270a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Musichen <alex.musichen@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:21:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] docs(blends-guide): the Blends guide describes the 1.0
 commands, templates and plugin folder

The site's own /docs/blends guide is written by hand (sync-sites does not touch it) and had drifted from the package:

- CLI reference: six verbs, not three (init, add, upgrade, plugins, build-client, check-deps, and kv import); init takes the six templates and --desktop; add copies into plugins/ and records plugins/library.lock.json, with --suite; upgrade is documented with --dry-run, --force and --diff.
- Templates: six, not three (blank, nodejs, notes, chat, todo, agent), all with one plugin folder, plugins/.
- The plugin library: src/plugins/ and extensions/ are one folder, plugins/; the acryl-door plugin is named; the duplicated "settings" sentence is removed.
- The app manifest and getting started: npm run lock writes blend.lock.json (it did not write acrylblends.lock.json), and 1.0's acrylblends upgrade is named where a reader needs it.
- The Blend registry and extending a running app: a starter and a plugin both ship under plugins/, not extensions/.
- The ACRYL framework: the class is Acryl, not App (removed in 1.0), and the page names the published entries (acrylblends/cordis/router, ...) as well as the app's own copies.
